      "description": "Wordmark left, small pill buttons right.",
      "html": "<header class=\"ds-nav\"><a class=\"ds-mark\" href=\"#\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 40 40\" width=\"36\" height=\"36\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"2\" width=\"8\" height=\"6\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffc93c\" stroke=\"#2b1b3d\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"23\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#cde7ff\" stroke=\"#2b1b3d\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M20 23 L20 14 M20 23 L26 26\" stroke=\"#2b1b3d\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg><span>Speed<span class=\"ds-mark-b\">rundle</span></span></a><nav><button class=\"ds-nb\" aria-label=\"Settings\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"3\"/><path d=\"M19.4 15a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33 1.82l.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83 2.83l-.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82-.33 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1 1.51V21a2 2 0 1 1-4 0v-.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1-1.51 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82.33l-.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83-2.83l.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33-1.82 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51-1H3a2 2 0 1 1 0-4h.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.51-1 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33-1.82l-.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83-2.83l.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82.33H9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1-1.51V3a2 2 0 1 1 4 0v.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1 1.51 1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82-.33l.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83 2.83l-.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33 1.82V9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.51 1H21a2 2 0 1 1 0 4h-.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51 1z\"/></svg></button></nav></header>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;padding:12px 16px;background:var(--cream,#fff8ee)}.ds-mark{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-family:var(--font-fredoka),Fredoka,ui-rounded,system-ui,sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.45rem;color:var(--ink,#2b1b3d);text-decoration:none}.ds-mark-b{color:#7a4fd6}.ds-nb{display:inline-grid;place-items:center;width:44px;height:44px;border:3px solid var(--ink,#2b1b3d);border-radius:999px;background:#fff;color:var(--ink,#2b1b3d);box-shadow:3px 3px 0 var(--ink,#2b1b3d);cursor:pointer;transition:transform 140ms cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1),box-shadow 140ms}.ds-nb:hover{transform:translate(-1px,-1px);box-shadow:4px 4px 0 var(--ink,#2b1b3d)}.ds-nb:active{transform:translate(3px,3px);box-shadow:none}.ds-nb:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--focus,#6a3df0);outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sticker Card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "sticker-card",
      "description": "The shared material: outlined slab with a hard plum lift.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-sticker\"><p class=\"ds-st-n\">5</p><p class=\"ds-st-l\">Day streak</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-sticker{display:inline-flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;padding:12px 16px;border:3px solid var(--ink,#2b1b3d);border-radius:18px;background:var(--butter,#fff0a8);color:var(--ink,#2b1b3d);box-shadow:4px 4px 0 var(--ink,#2b1b3d);transform:rotate(-2deg)}.ds-st-n{margin:0;font-family:var(--font-fredoka),Fredoka,ui-rounded,sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:2rem;line-height:1}.ds-st-l{margin:4px 0 0;font-family:var(--font-nunito),Nunito,sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:.875rem}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Split Strip",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "split-strip",
      "description": "Signature: a run as plum-separated candy blocks sized by time; gold best split, hatched skip.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-strip\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Wordle 1:24, Connections 1:59 best, NYT Mini skipped, Spelling Bee 7:19\"><div class=\"ds-b\" style=\"flex-grow:84;background:#c8f0dc\"></div><div class=\"ds-b\" style=\"flex-grow:119;background:#ffc93c\"><span>&#9733; 1:59</span></div><div class=\"ds-b ds-hatch\" style=\"flex-grow:40\"></div><div class=\"ds-b\" style=\"flex-grow:439;background:#ffd9c2\"><span>7:19</span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-strip{display:flex;height:48px;overflow:hidden;border:3px solid var(--ink,#2b1b3d);border-radius:999px;background:#fff;box-shadow:4px 4px 0 var(--ink,#2b1b3d)}.ds-b{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-basis:0;min-width:12px;font-family:var(--font-fredoka),Fredoka,ui-rounded,sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:.875rem;color:var(--ink,#2b1b3d)}.ds-b+.ds-b{border-left:3px solid var(--ink,#2b1b3d)}.ds-hatch{background-color:var(--cream-deep,#fbecd6);background-image:repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg,rgb(43 27 61/.28) 0 2px,transparent 2px 7px)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Gold Chip",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "gold-chip",
      "description": "Marks a best split or delta; gold only for bests.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-gold\"><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path fill=\"#2b1b3d\" d=\"M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z\"/></svg>-0:12.4</span>",
      "css": ".ds-gold{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;padding:0 8px;border:2px solid var(--ink,#2b1b3d);border-radius:999px;background:var(--gold,#ffc93c);color:var(--ink,#2b1b3d);font-family:var(--font-fredoka),Fredoka,ui-rounded,sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:.875rem}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Candy Shop Split Strip",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Candy Shop Split Strip\"**\n\nSpeedrundle is a sticker sheet on a cream counter. Every surface is a die-cut sticker: a white or pastel slab with a 3px plum outline and a hard 4px plum shadow offset down and to the right, which presses flat when tapped. The ground is warm cream with a faint 22px plum dot grid, so the page reads as paper rather than screen. Six candy pastels give each game its own colour, plum carries all text and every outline, and gold is held back for one job: marking a personal best.\n\nThe signature is the split strip. A run is drawn as a pill of coloured blocks, one per game, separated by plum rules. The same strip appears as live run progress (equal blocks), as the result (blocks sized by time, gold for best splits, hatched for skipped), on the dashboard as the latest run, and stacked vertically as the bars of the 14-day chart. New surfaces that show a run show it this way.\n\nThe world is playful but phone-first and morning-tired: big round tap targets (48px minimum), one dominant action per screen, rounded type, and an original stopwatch mascot. It is light only. It refuses the grey stopwatch app and the stat-tile SaaS dashboard.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cream dotted ground, plum ink, six game pastels, gold for bests only.",
      "3px plum outlines and 4px hard offset shadows that press flat on tap.",
      "Generous radius: 12px fields, 18px stickers, 28px hero button, pills for buttons and the strip.",
      "Fredoka for display and numerals (through equal-width digit boxes), Nunito for body and tables.",
      "The split strip is the one shape every run takes.",
      "Light only; reduced motion turns off all decorative movement."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Gold Means Best Rule",
        "body": "Gold (#ffc93c) marks a personal best or a best split and nothing else. It is never a game colour, a decoration, or a generic highlight.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never Colour Alone Rule",
        "body": "The pastels are too close to identify games by hue and fail a categorical-chart check. Game identity is always carried by something else too: plum separators between blocks, a named readout under the chart, a labelled table row, a named dot list, and diagonal hatching for skipped splits.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Dusk Plum Floor Rule",
        "body": "Secondary text is Dusk Plum (#5b4670) or darker, never a lighter tint, so it holds AA on cream, every pastel and gold.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Equal Digit Rule",
        "body": "Fredoka has no tabular figures. Every Fredoka time readout (timer, strip labels, result rows, stat stickers, chart readout) renders through the digit-box treatment: each digit in a 0.62em centred box, separators at natural width, so ticking numbers never jitter. Do not rely on `tabular-nums` with Fredoka; it does nothing.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Table Voice Rule",
        "body": "Columns of times in tables use Nunito with tabular-nums, not Fredoka, so they align as a column.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Press Flat Rule",
        "body": "Anything with a lift is tappable or is a record sticker; on press it translates by the full lift distance and its shadow drops to zero. Disabled controls keep their shadow but sit at 50% opacity and do not move.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** give every tappable surface or record sticker the 3px plum outline and a hard offset shadow (4px plum by default, gold under plum buttons) that presses flat on tap.",
      "**Do** draw any run as the split strip: plum-separated blocks in game pastels, gold for best splits, hatch for skipped.",
      "**Do** pair every use of a game pastel with a name, a label, a plum separator or hatching.",
      "**Do** render Fredoka times through the 0.62em equal digit boxes, and table times in Nunito with tabular-nums.",
      "**Do** keep secondary text at Dusk Plum (#5b4670) or darker.",
      "**Do** keep tap targets at 44px or more, 48px for standard buttons and fields.",
      "**Do** gate every decorative animation and confetti behind prefers-reduced-motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use gold for anything but personal bests and best splits.",
      "**Don't** identify a game by pastel colour alone.",
      "**Don't** use blurred or ambient shadows; depth here is hard and offset.",
      "**Don't** add a dark mode; the system is light only.",
      "**Don't** set Fredoka numerals that change in place without equal digit boxes.",
      "**Don't** use the games' logos or artwork; game art is original illustration on the game's pastel."
    ]
  }
}